    "hello_walk_width_m": 2.42,
    "evidence": "The University of Oregon library identifies the fountain as the Class of 1913 gift. The 2025 Fenton Hall survey identifies Hello Walk and records the missing spout. County orthophotos establish the stepped stone outline, exposed path sections and the junction south of University Hall. The centerline between exposed sections is estimated beneath trees. The 2007 survey photograph establishes the recessed basin and circular bowl on four feet. The heights and dry basin finish are estimates.",
